postgresql-common — installed as: postgresql-common
Licence declared by Alpine: MIT

The scripts that select which installed PostgreSQL major version the client commands run.

Written by the Alpine Linux project. It has no upstream source: its source is the aport
itself, https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports/-/tree/3.24-stable/main/postgresql-common, which contains no licence file and no copyright notice. Alpine declares
MIT for it, and no copyright notice has been published for it, so none is reproduced here.
